(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until"] [4 1 "// the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops"] [5 1 "// it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,"] [6 1 "// else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it."] [8 1 "// guardedStep is step with a Go panic of the runtime turned into a SystemError raised at f's instruction"] [9 1 "// (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core, PY6a's Low: a panic ended the whole lib-test module, now only its test)"] [14 31 "// the C-level checks' increments the panic skipped"] [15 31 "// and a direct call's (queue 216d), had the panic crossed one"] [20 3 "// step's own frame not entered for compiled code (queue 216d); while tracing, the loop (queue 219t): a compiled"] [21 3 "// frame hands itself over at a block start (AotToLoop)"] [29 1 "// run runs f (and the frames it calls) to f's return: Go's call into the machine, CPython's"] [30 1 "// _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault entered from C, the C level's recursion check first (where \"\", PY7)."] [41 1 "// runFrames is run's loop, f its entry frame. direct (queue 216d): f is a callee a compiled caller runs from its own Go"] [42 1 "// code (callDirect) where it would have returned f as its *pushFrame: f entered as this loop enters a pushed frame,"] [43 1 "// the eval breaker's error raised in f, and no C level counted (a Python call is none: run's check is Go's entry)."] [47 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [55 31 "// a direct callee's RESUME error, raised in it as in a pushed frame"] [56 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [66 40 "// sys.monitoring's PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW (queue 220)"] [78 37 "// PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD (queue 220): a callback's error raised in f"] [82 4 "// f returned v"] [90 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [98 5 "// callInit's __init__ returned: the instance is the call's value (type_call's check of __init__'s)"] [111 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [123 25 "// PY_START (queue 220), its error raised in the callee"] [132 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee"] [140 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [147 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [152 23 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [156 38 "// RAISE (queue 219t): settrace's 'exception'"] [165 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [171 24 "// PY_UNWIND (queue 220)"] [184 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [185 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [186 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [189 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [190 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [193 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [201 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [204 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [205 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [206 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [207 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [209 22 "// sys.monitoring's CALL, C_RETURN, C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [221 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [233 4 "// a built-in method bound to its object (BuiltinType's call slot): its arguments made at once with self"] [234 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [263 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [270 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [271 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [272 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [275 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [276 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [277 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [286 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [287 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [288 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [289 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [290 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [291 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] [301 1 "// runDirect is callDirect's run of callee from the running frame's compiled code: its value (callInit's instance for"] [302 1 "// an __init__), or its exception, returned to that code."] [321 1 "// callInit is the call of a class whose __init__ runs in the caller's loop (initInline; queue 210, CPython 3.14's"] [322 1 "// CALL_ALLOC_AND_ENTER_INIT): the instance made by the type's __new__ (object's) from the arguments where they are"] [323 1 "// on f's stack (k the first's position), then __init__'s frame with the instance as self in the class's slot,"] [324 1 "// returned as the thread's *pushFrame; runFrames pushes the instance when that frame returns None (TypeType's call"] [325 1 "// slot's check otherwise, raised at the call)."] [343 1 "// initInline is the __init__ a call of t (its metatype type) runs in the caller's loop (callInit): the Python"] [344 1 "// function __init__ resolves to, when t and every class of its MRO but object are class statements' (no built-in"] [345 1 "// layout), __new__ resolves to object's and __init__ is not a generator's or a coroutine's; nil otherwise, and the"] [346 1 "// call goes through TypeType's call slot. Kept on t while typeEpoch has not moved."] [374 1 "// kwnamesAt is a call's keyword names, the tuple constant i of str (-1: none), made once."] [396 1 "// step runs f's instructions until it returns (the value, nil), raises (nil, error), or calls a"] [397 1 "// Python function (nil, *pushFrame)."] [401 3 "// compiled ahead (PY8, aot.go): the same frame, from f.PC; while tracing, the loop (queue 219t)"] [407 36 "// the line, opcode and jump events (queue 219t, trace.go)"] [766 24 "// CALL, and a C callable's C_RETURN or C_RAISE (queue 220)"] [787 6 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [826 33 "// a function made where the globals are a mapping has them too (func_globals)"] [845 52 "// JUMP_BACKWARD: the eval breaker"] [876 24 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [898 5 "// RERAISE N: the lasti N items down is where the frame reports itself (f_lineno)"] [904 4 "// the traceback continues: the handler's frame is already in it"] [938 3 "// globals not a dict but a subclass's instance (FunctionType(code, globals), exec, eval; queue 205f): its"] [939 3 "// __getitem__, a KeyError not found (LOAD_GLOBAL's and LOAD_FROM_DICT_OR_GLOBALS' PyMapping_GetOptionalItem)"] [950 1 "// globalIC is load-global's inline cache (queue 210; CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL_MODULE and LOAD_GLOBAL_BUILTIN, by the"] [951 1 "// dicts' keys version): the globals it last saw and where the name was: in the globals at entry gi, or (gi -1)"] [952 1 "// absent from them at their version gver and in the builtins b at entry bi. An entry is the name's while it holds"] [953 1 "// the name's very str (names are interned: co_names, and a module's and the builtins' names, through nameStr), so a"] [954 1 "// hit reads the entry's current value; the globals' absence holds while their version, moved by every insertion and"] [955 1 "// deletion, has not."] [962 1 "// loadGlobalAt is load-global of name at f's instruction pc (loadGlobal through the instruction's cache)."] [1012 1 "// loadNameGlobal is LOAD_NAME's lookup after the locals: the globals' dict itself (_PyEval_LoadName's"] [1013 1 "// PyDict_GetItemRef: a dict subclass's __missing__ not called), then the builtins."] [1037 1 "// doRaise is raise (0: re-raise the handled exception; 1: raise exc; 2: raise exc from cause)."] [1067 1 "// makeException is raise's operand as an exception: an instance, or a class called with no arguments."] [1086 1 "// exceptionMatches is except's test: exc an instance of typ, or of one of a tuple's types."] [1106 1 "// unpackExactly is a target list's items: n of them or a ValueError."] [1117 4 "// unpack_iterable: only a type with no iteration at all is \"non-iterable\"; __iter__'s own error propagates"] [1146 1 "// Contains is v in container."] [1166 1 "// SetItem is o[k] = v, or del o[k] when v is nil."] [1168 2 "// an exact list's item at an int in range set (202b, GetItem's)"] [1190 1 "// GetItemOrNil is m[k] for a namespace's lookup: nil when absent (a KeyError swallowed)."] [1205 1 "// dictMergeKwargs is DICT_MERGE: m's items into d (a call's **m), a repeated keyword a TypeError."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[13 20] [19 16] [22 29] [60 40] [83 35] [97 25] [110 34] [125 28] [160 37] [210 48] [220 46] [226 36] [227 30] [232 35] [331 60] [365 31] [382 23] [402 30] [408 29] [478 43] [491 42] [498 62] [501 60] [509 57] [528 54] [602 14] [602 30] [603 42] [612 24] [628 59] [634 63] [642 30] [650 63] [655 25] [658 63] [665 45] [672 30] [682 18] [682 32] [686 23] [686 31] [693 30] [699 32] [710 38] [728 31] [767 65] [776 49] [781 37] [807 27] [807 35] [819 63] [846 35] [875 30] [897 21] [899 47] [975 22] [978 28] [979 22] [1044 42] [1056 44] [1078 30] [1118 29] [1148 41] [1160 25] [1169 23] [1170 23] [1181 32] [1192 23] [1197 28] [1224 26] [1231 25]]} (go/file "eval.go" :imports [])

